\section{Introduction}
Dhuwaya (ISO 639-3 dwy) is a Yolngu Matha variety of north-east Arnhem Land. Search results describe it as the first language of children at Yirrkala School, where it is used in a long-running bilingual programme.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Yirrkala School's Literature Production Centre and the Yolngu bilingual programme (reported as 90\% Yolngu Matha in early grades falling to 10\% in older grades): \url{https://aeunt.org.au/yirrkala-lpc-team-recognised-for-contribution-to-atsi-education}
\item NT Department of Education item on the Yirrkala language centre: \url{https://education.nt.gov.au/statistics-research-and-strategies/indigenous-education-strategy/indigenous-education-strategy-issue-17/yirrkala-language-centre-recognised}
\end{itemize}

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Bilingual education in Australian Aboriginal communities: the forty years of the Yirrkala step model (academic): \url{https://scholarspace.manoa.hawaii.edu/items/5543ce9a-c96b-4eb4-ae4d-03204e0156ef/full}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Indigenous Languages and Arts / ILF news on the launch of \emph{Wanhaka yothu yingai} in Yirrkala: \url{https://www.ilf.org.au/news/launch-of-wanhaka-yothu-yingai-in-yirrkala}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item SBS podcast episode, ``50 years strong: bilingual teaching is celebrated in Yirrkala'': \url{https://phoenix.mkoga-1.edsqa01.aws.sbs.com.au/news/podcast-episode/50-years-strong-bilingual-teaching-is-celebrated-in-yirrkala/y5342zpfh}
\end{itemize}

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Yirrkala School runs a staircase-model bilingual programme with Dhuwaya as the main Yolngu language. Search results gave no individual textbook titles or downloadable materials, so those should be requested from the school's Literature Production Centre.
\end{document}
